build: 2026-06-24 v10.76.20 (Bio→Visual restored — launch metadata overflow fixed at the source)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: 10.76.19 launched + ran a full session (confirmed on device), proving the launch
  brick was the Bio→Visual feature, not the build. This re-adds Bio→Visual WITH the real
  fix. Root cause (proven by 10.76.18 == 10.76.9 launching): soundControls is built in the
  main scroll at LAUNCH, and its compiled SwiftUI type was the SUM of all 7 inlined panel
  sub-types. visualPanel gained the Bio→Visual section in 10.76.10, pushing that summed
  type past the Swift runtime metadata decoder's recursion limit → SIGSEGV / black screen.
  10.76.9 sat just under the limit. (My earlier .15/.16/.17 fixes missed it — they erased
  the fullscreen cover, which only builds when you OPEN the visual, not at launch.)
  FIX: AnyView-erase each of the 7 panels in soundControls AND visualPanel's deep children
  (visualLookStrip / visualBlendControls / visualPresetRow / musicColourRow /
  bioVisualSection). Each now decodes as its own shallow type with lots of headroom, so
  this class of crash can't recur as panels grow. Reviewed (compile-safe + sufficient).
  Bio→Visual feature is back: route body channels (HR/HRV/breath/coherence/motion) or an
  LFO to the visual params (intensity/detail/motion/spread/hue/saturation/Blend morph).
  Test: still launches, and Sound ▸ Visual panel shows the "Bio → Visual" routing again.
  (Separately noted from your log: the rPPG BPM is jittery/octave-jumpy — that's the next
  task once this is confirmed; it does not affect launch.)
